WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:02.480
An alien with a horse head.

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:03.580
The "Frog of Thunder."

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:05.600
A couple of mutants.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:09.720
Heroes from the future and other universes,
even the DC universe.

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:15.300
When it comes to Marvel Comics, Thor Odinson
isn't the only one who's been worthy of wielding

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:16.300
the hammer.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:24.169
First appearing in 1962's Journey Into Mystery
#83, Thor Odinson is initially the alter ego

00:00:24.169 --> 00:00:29.800
of Dr. Donald Blake, who finds Mjolnir and
proves worthy to wield it.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:34.000
Thor and Blake can switch places by smacking
Mjolnir on the ground.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:38.920
It's later revealed that Blake is a construct
of Thor's father Odin, and while there are

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:43.750
a few other attempts to saddle Thor with a
secret identity, for the most part, he exists

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:45.380
solely as Thor.

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:50.940
Even during periods when Thor Odinson briefly
loses his powers, he never stays on the sidelines

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:52.390
for very long.

00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:56.030
Even without Mjolnir, he refuses to be anything
but a hero.

00:00:56.030 --> 00:00:58.079
"At least make it a challenge for me!"

00:00:58.733 --> 00:01:05.530
When the Ultimate Thor is introduced in 2002's
Ultimates #4, no one's sure if he really is

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:06.530
Thor.

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:10.860
Nick Fury tries to recruit him into the Ultimates
while he's a far-left activist in Norway who

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:14.710
has published self-help books and is popular
on lecture circuits.

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:19.960
He was also institutionalized for over a year
after his revelation that he was the Son of

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:20.960
Odin.

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:24.750
It isn't until the second Ultimates volume
that his godhood is confirmed.

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:29.799
The Ultimate Thor is one of the many heroes
lost when Marvel's Ultimate line officially

00:01:29.799 --> 00:01:32.560
closed with 2015's Ultimate End.

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:38.430
His unique version of Mjolnir remains, though,
as this half-hammer, half-ax appears in Asgard

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:43.439
at the end of 2015's Thors miniseries and
has since had a significant impact on the

00:01:43.439 --> 00:01:45.909
course of events in the prime Marvel Universe.

00:01:46.909 --> 00:01:53.310
As a result of the 2014 line-wide event "Original
Sin," Thor Odinson loses his worthiness.

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:58.770
In that year's Thor #1, a female Thor takes
up the hammer and fills the void that Odinson

00:01:58.770 --> 00:01:59.770
leaves behind.

00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:05.390
Her identity was left a mystery for a time,
but eventually Thor's former main squeeze

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:10.550
Jane Foster is revealed to be the new hammer-wielder
in Thor #8.

00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:12.020
"Jane?!"

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:14.770
Jane then remains Thor for four years.

00:02:14.770 --> 00:02:21.610
In 2018's Mighty Thor #705, she's forced to
sacrifice Mjolnir in order to defeat the monster

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:25.210
Mangog, thereby losing the power of Thor.

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:31.030
More recently, in the conclusion to 2019's
"War of the Realms" event, Jane replaces Valkyrie

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:33.770
in the ongoing series Valkyrie: Jane Foster.

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:39.420
Walt Simonson's run on Thor remains one of
the most well-remembered stints in Marvel

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:40.720
Comics history.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:46.110
That includes his introduction of horse-faced
hero Beta Ray Bill, who proves himself worthy

00:02:46.110 --> 00:02:48.380
of the power of Thor.

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:55.900
In 1983's Thor #337, Thor intercepts a spaceship
at Nick Fury's request, but its pilot turns

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:56.930
violent.

00:02:56.930 --> 00:03:01.760
During their clash, Bill lifts Mjolnir, only
seeking to use it against Thor.

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:06.660
They eventually work things out, and Odin
decrees that since Bill has proven himself

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:10.910
worthy, he and Thor must fight for Mjolnir's
possession.

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:14.230
Bill wins the fight, but refuses to take the
hammer.

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:20.030
So instead, Odin has the dwarves of Nidavellir
create a new hammer named Stormbreaker for

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:21.030
Bill.

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:29.920
In 1978's Thor #276, cameraman Roger "Red"
Norvell captures Thor Odinson's belt of strength

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:34.950
and iron gloves, allowing him to become a
new Thor capable of wielding Mjolnir.

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:40.130
The new red-haired Thor seems more villain
than hero at first, but he eventually proves

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:45.790
himself worthy of the title when he sacrifices
himself to save Asgard two issues later.

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:47.750
And that isn't the end of Red Norvell.

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:54.580
He earns a spot in Valhalla for his sacrifice,
and Odin resurrects him in Thor #478 to replace

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:58.470
Thor, whom Odin feels is neglecting his duties
to Asgard.

00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:04.100
Since then, Red has essentially been in limbo,
as he was last seen in 1997's Journey Into

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:05.865
Mystery #513.

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:12.800
In "The Asgardian Wars," stretched across
1985's New Mutants Special Edition #1 and

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:19.079
X-Men Annual #9, Loki tempts Storm from the
X-Men by giving her what seems to be the power

00:04:19.079 --> 00:04:20.079
of Thor.

00:04:20.079 --> 00:04:24.630
When her friends arrive on Asgard to save
her, Loki's magic makes them all appear as

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:25.630
enemies.

00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:31.310
Loki crafts a powerful hammer for Ororo, and
she nearly kills Wolverine with its magic

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:33.900
and gives Hela a run for her money.

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:39.460
Eventually, Ororo sees through Loki's magic
and relinquishes her power, knowing that keeping

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:42.250
it would mean being Loki's puppet.

00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:46.710
Despite this sacrifice, "The Asgardian Wars"
isn't the last appearance of this particular

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:52.927
goddess of thunder, as she's shown to still
have access to this power in 2018's X-Men:

00:04:52.927 --> 00:04:53.804
Gold #26.

00:04:54.372 --> 00:04:57.771
"Do you know what happens to a toad when it's
struck by lightning?"

00:04:57.771 --> 00:05:01.911
"The same thing that happens to everyone else."

00:05:03.229 --> 00:05:07.960
If you've ever wondered what Thor would look
like in a dystopian future, then you'd better

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:16.069
check out 1987's Thor #384, in which Dargo
Ktor is transformed into a much spikier version

00:05:16.069 --> 00:05:17.069
of our hero.

00:05:17.069 --> 00:05:23.030
In the 26th century, a massive corporation
called Corp rules over the Earth.

00:05:23.030 --> 00:05:28.330
Dargo is a member of the secretive Cult of
the Hammer that somehow manages to locate

00:05:28.330 --> 00:05:32.080
Mjolnir, though he doesn't believe in stories
of thunder gods.

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:38.270
When Loki uses the forces of Corp to assault
the Cult, Dargo grasps Mjolnir's handle and

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:40.159
proves himself worthy.

00:05:40.159 --> 00:05:45.500
Dargo also appears again a few more times,
including as a member of the original Thor

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:46.031
Corps.

00:05:46.784 --> 00:05:55.020
At the very end of 1986's Thor #363, a disguised
Loki turns his half-brother into a frog.

00:05:55.020 --> 00:06:00.669
Thor remains froggy for a few issues, thereby
becoming Throg, Frog of Thunder.

00:06:00.669 --> 00:06:03.770
Then in 2009, a new Throg emerged.

00:06:03.770 --> 00:06:10.169
In Lockjaw &amp; the Pet Avengers #1, we meet
Simon Walterson, who's cursed by a witch and

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:12.840
becomes Throg full time.

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:15.099
He's become kind of popular since then.

00:06:15.099 --> 00:06:20.689
You can croak fear into the hearts of your
enemies as Throg in LEGO Marvel Super-Heroes

00:06:20.689 --> 00:06:26.610
2, and he also had his own story in 2017's
Mighty Thor #700.

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:32.639
More recently, Throg kicked interstellar butt
as the tiniest member of the Asgardians of

00:06:32.639 --> 00:06:37.280
the Galaxy, and he also showed up very briefly
on the Loki TV show.

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:38.280
"Ugh!

00:06:38.897 --> 00:06:39.897
Ahh!"

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:47.240
For a time, Thor maintained the secret identity
Sigurd Janson, whose closest circle of friends

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:49.370
included Eric Masterson.

00:06:49.370 --> 00:06:55.840
In 1989's Thor #408, Thor begs his father
to save Masterson's life after he's fatally

00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:58.349
wounded by the villain Mongoose.

00:06:58.349 --> 00:07:02.969
Odin solves the problem by using his magic
to merge Thor and Eric together.

00:07:02.969 --> 00:07:08.279
When they're eventually separated, Odin creates
the mace Thunderstrike for Eric, granting

00:07:08.279 --> 00:07:11.030
him abilities comparable to Thor's.

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:14.320
Eric names himself Thunderstrike after the
mace.

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:19.520
Unfortunately, he ultimately makes the mistake
of using a weapon called the Bloodaxe, as

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:21.729
it possesses him with its power.

00:07:21.729 --> 00:07:27.850
In 1995's Thunderstrike #24, he regains control
of himself long enough to make the ultimate

00:07:27.850 --> 00:07:30.819
sacrifice in order to defeat the Bloodaxe.

00:07:32.110 --> 00:07:37.240
A decade before Jane Foster proved herself
worthy, there was Thor Girl.

00:07:37.240 --> 00:07:43.080
Her real name is Tarene, an alien gifted with
cosmic powers whose coming was foretold billions

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:45.789
of years ago by an alien sorcerer.

00:07:45.789 --> 00:07:52.639
She uses her abilities to turn herself into
an Asgardian goddess in 2001's Thor #33.

00:07:52.639 --> 00:07:58.259
For a time, she acts as Thor Odinson's ally,
but she eventually loses most of her power

00:07:58.259 --> 00:08:00.279
in battle with the demon Surtur.

00:08:00.279 --> 00:08:03.530
Tarene then remains on the periphery of the
Marvel Universe.

00:08:03.530 --> 00:08:08.509
She becomes a part of the government's Initiative
project during "Civil War" and even battles

00:08:08.509 --> 00:08:13.909
the Hulk and his Warbound in the 2007 event
"World War Hulk."

00:08:13.909 --> 00:08:18.990
She's last seen in a later event, "Fear Itself,"
during which she grows tired of humanity and

00:08:18.990 --> 00:08:20.610
leaves Earth for spaceways.

00:08:22.067 --> 00:08:27.750
After the events of 2015's "Secret Wars,"
the Ultimate Thor's version of Mjolnir appears

00:08:27.750 --> 00:08:29.659
in Old Asgard.

00:08:29.659 --> 00:08:35.390
Thor Odinson initially seems to want to retrieve
the weapon for himself in the miniseries "Unworthy

00:08:35.390 --> 00:08:38.620
Thor," but he eventually decides it isn't
for him.

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:44.450
We learn in Mighty Thor #20 that Volstagg,
the large, red-haired member of the Warriors

00:08:44.450 --> 00:08:46.680
Three, takes up the hammer instead.

00:08:46.680 --> 00:08:51.080
He then becomes the War Thor shortly after
he's traumatized when he fails to save a group

00:08:51.080 --> 00:08:53.280
of children from a fire demon.

00:08:53.280 --> 00:09:00.230
When Volstagg tries and fails to stop the
monster Mangog in 2017's Mighty Thor #701,

00:09:00.230 --> 00:09:05.850
the beast crushes the Ultimate version of
Mjolnir and leaves Volstagg bleeding and helpless.

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:09.740
“If you even think about betraying him…”

00:09:09.740 --> 00:09:11.430
“You’ll…kill me?

00:09:11.430 --> 00:09:13.482
Evidently, there will be a line.”

00:09:15.340 --> 00:09:18.530
The third issue of Civil War ends with a bit
of a shocker.

00:09:18.530 --> 00:09:23.310
Thor had been missing and presumed dead, but
he appears on the last page ready to do some

00:09:23.310 --> 00:09:24.310
damage.

00:09:24.310 --> 00:09:27.580
In the following issue, he kills Bill Foster,
a.k.a.

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:28.580
Goliath.

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:34.270
We later learn that this is not Thor but a
cyborg clone, and the mythic warrior Hercules

00:09:34.270 --> 00:09:38.440
crushes the clone's head with his own hammer
in Civil War #7.

00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:46.010
The clone later awakens in 2009's Avengers:
The Initiative #21 and renames himself Ragnarok.

00:09:46.010 --> 00:09:50.690
He spends some years as a villain, recruited
into the villainous Green Goblin's team of

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:54.260
Dark Avengers, and then he eventually joins
the Thunderbolts.

00:09:54.260 --> 00:10:00.310
He was last seen in 2013's Dark Avengers #190
on a mission on an alternate Earth.

00:10:01.492 --> 00:10:06.540
After the death of Eric Masterson, his mace
is left in the hands of the Avengers.

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:12.950
In 2010's Thunderstrike #1, Captain America
gives the mace to Eric's son Kevin.

00:10:12.950 --> 00:10:17.030
After using the weapon to try to pry some
civilians loose when they're pinned under

00:10:17.030 --> 00:10:22.280
a car, Kevin experiences the same transformation
as his late father.

00:10:22.280 --> 00:10:27.760
After a short solo series, Kevin joins the
young "Avengers Academy" heroes, fighting

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:32.150
alongside them in the 2011 line-wide event
"Fear Itself."

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:35.470
He then later joins the ranks of the Asgardians
of the Galaxy.

00:10:36.770 --> 00:10:41.760
Often appearing more like Odin than Thor,
King Thor has one eye, one arm, and little

00:10:41.760 --> 00:10:44.260
patience for his younger counterparts.

00:10:44.260 --> 00:10:49.850
He joins the Thor of the present and the Thor
of the past to help defeat Gorr the God Butcher,

00:10:49.850 --> 00:10:53.950
and later reunites with them in the 2019 event
"War of the Realms."

00:10:53.950 --> 00:10:58.910
King Thor remains a constant throughout Jason
Aaron's tenure on Thor, and we eventually

00:10:58.910 --> 00:11:04.000
see the Thor of the present suffer the wounds
that are old news to King Thor.

00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:09.140
In June 2019, Marvel announced that Aaron
would conclude his time writing Thor with

00:11:09.140 --> 00:11:13.850
the four-part miniseries "King Thor," focusing
primarily on this future Odinson.

00:11:13.850 --> 00:11:16.500
"So I like a lot of different Thors.

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:18.230
I don't think we have to pick just one."

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:21.780
Thor wasn't always worthy of Mjolnir.

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:26.440
Impatient for his chance with the hammer,
the young Thor is often seen testing his ability

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:30.350
to lift the hammer, only to curse at it when
he fails.

00:11:30.350 --> 00:11:35.280
Without Mjolnir, the youthful Thor carries
the powerful ax Jarnbjorn.

00:11:35.280 --> 00:11:40.870
Unfortunately, it can't grant Thor the gift
of flight like Mjolnir, so instead he rides

00:11:40.870 --> 00:11:43.860
a chariot pulled by his two flying goats.

00:11:43.860 --> 00:11:49.310
This younger, ax-wielding Odinson aids the
present-day Thor both in his battle against

00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:54.430
the God Butcher and his final conflict with
Malekith in "War of the Realms."

00:11:55.810 --> 00:12:00.990
In the 2018 Marvel event "Infinity Wars,"
a separate universe is created in the Soul

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:05.990
Stone whose inhabitants are the combination
of pre-existing Marvel characters.

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:11.920
In particular, the stories of Iron Man and
Thor merge to become that of Stark Odinson,

00:12:11.920 --> 00:12:13.530
the Iron Hammer.

00:12:13.530 --> 00:12:18.390
Almost all of the villains, friends, and lovers
of both Thor and Iron Man are combined to

00:12:18.390 --> 00:12:21.530
create the cast of Iron Hammer's stories.

00:12:21.530 --> 00:12:27.880
Madame Masque and Hela, for example, are combined
to make Madame Hel, while the dark elf Kurse

00:12:27.880 --> 00:12:32.240
and Crimson Dynamo come together as the Krimson
Kurse.

00:12:32.240 --> 00:12:36.030
Iron Hammer was last seen in 2019's "Secret
Warps" event.

00:12:37.730 --> 00:12:42.450
As you can probably tell, it's not unusual
for a handful of different people to simultaneously

00:12:42.450 --> 00:12:46.560
call themselves "Thor" or at least to claim
some of his power.

00:12:46.560 --> 00:12:52.540
But in 1993 that was still relatively novel,
and that was when Marvel launched the miniseries

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:53.540
Thor Corps.

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:59.040
The storyline united Thor Odinson, Beta Ray
Bill, the original Thunderstrike, and Dargo

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:02.290
the 26th century Thor all on one team.

00:13:02.290 --> 00:13:07.850
The four embark on an adventure that sees
them saving reality itself and battling villains

00:13:07.850 --> 00:13:09.870
and heroes from all over the multiverse.

00:13:09.870 --> 00:13:15.660
It would be over two decades before the phrase
"Thor Corps" became regularly heard in the

00:13:15.660 --> 00:13:20.630
comics vernacular again, and this time it
was a very different group of Thors with a

00:13:20.630 --> 00:13:22.390
much larger roster.

00:13:23.390 --> 00:13:29.240
In the 2015 event "Secret Wars," Doctor Doom
creates a patchwork planet called Battleworld

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:33.880
with alternate reality versions of different
characters sharing the same planet.

00:13:33.880 --> 00:13:39.350
For his police force, "God" Doom creates a
new version of the Thor Corps, which includes

00:13:39.350 --> 00:13:42.380
hundreds of Thors from across the multiverse.

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:47.140
There are familiar characters like Ultimate
Thor and Beta Ray Bill, alongside tons of

00:13:47.140 --> 00:13:52.970
new versions like a Gamora Thor, a Lizard
Thor, and even a Groot Thor who says only

00:13:52.970 --> 00:13:54.450
"I am Thor."

00:13:54.450 --> 00:13:55.800
"You speak Groot?"

00:13:55.800 --> 00:13:58.490
"Yes, they taught it on Asgard as an elective."

00:13:58.490 --> 00:14:04.570
The Thors take center stage in the miniseries
Thors, during which the Ultimate Thor investigates

00:14:04.570 --> 00:14:08.670
a string of serial murders of different Jane
Fosters across Battleworld.

00:14:08.670 --> 00:14:14.030
The series ends with the Thor Corps joining
the battle against God Doom, the death of

00:14:14.030 --> 00:14:18.410
the Ultimate Thor, and the Ultimate Mjolnir
appearing in Old Asgard.

00:14:20.530 --> 00:14:25.220
On Earth-928 in the year 2099, Thor is worshiped
once more.

00:14:25.220 --> 00:14:30.540
Along with his fellow Asgardians, Thor left
years earlier in response to the corporation

00:14:30.540 --> 00:14:33.840
Alchemax stoking anti-hero rage.

00:14:33.840 --> 00:14:38.600
Those who couldn't escape to different worlds
either ended up dead or quit being a hero.

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:43.960
The Church of Thor and its followers, known
as Thorites, wait anxiously for the return

00:14:43.960 --> 00:14:45.520
of the God of Thunder.

00:14:45.520 --> 00:14:50.710
But unbeknownst to the Thorites, Thor and
nearly all other Asgardians have already been

00:14:50.710 --> 00:14:51.930
killed.

00:14:51.930 --> 00:14:54.460
Only Loki survived by running and hiding.

00:14:54.460 --> 00:15:02.170
In Punisher 2099 #13, Alchemax engineers its
own Asgardians to act as the true gods returned

00:15:02.170 --> 00:15:03.170
to Earth.

00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:09.390
Cecil McAdam, a janitor at the Church, willingly
allows the corporation to turn him into their

00:15:09.390 --> 00:15:11.400
version of the Thunder God.

00:15:11.400 --> 00:15:16.590
He's genuinely motivated by a desire to be
heroic, but his corporate masters use him

00:15:16.590 --> 00:15:19.600
to distract from their dark dealings.

00:15:19.600 --> 00:15:25.770
When separated from his hammer, McAdam chooses
to chase it into an explosion, seemingly dying,

00:15:25.770 --> 00:15:27.670
rather than return to an ordinary life.

00:15:29.050 --> 00:15:35.360
The Marvel 2099 universe wasn't quite done
with Thor after Reverend McAdam's demise.

00:15:35.360 --> 00:15:40.150
In an echo of his Silver Age return, Captain
America was once again discovered in a block

00:15:40.150 --> 00:15:44.940
of ice after years of being assumed killed
in the superhero purge.

00:15:44.940 --> 00:15:50.430
Around the same time, Alchemax located the
true hammer of Thor, Mjolnir.

00:15:50.430 --> 00:15:55.190
Steve Rogers proves worthy and is able to
hoist the hammer, thereby becoming a heroic

00:15:55.190 --> 00:15:56.700
Thor for the era.

00:15:56.700 --> 00:16:01.921
Together with Spider-Man and a league of other
heroes in 2099: Manifest Destiny #1, they

00:16:01.921 --> 00:16:05.420
begin to repair the fallen world of 2099.

00:16:05.420 --> 00:16:10.730
This one-shot story marks the original end
of the 2099 line, as it sends the universe

00:16:10.730 --> 00:16:12.540
off on an upbeat note.

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:19.210
Marvel has typically depicted the Asgardian
apocalypse of Ragnarok as a localized event.

00:16:19.210 --> 00:16:24.200
Readers have watched the event destroy Asgard
and the gods several times, all without doing

00:16:24.200 --> 00:16:27.380
much damage to Midgard, aka Earth.

00:16:27.380 --> 00:16:28.620
But in What If?

00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:32.030
Age of Ultron #3, Earth is not spared.

00:16:32.030 --> 00:16:37.570
After slaying Thor and destroying Asgard,
the monstrous serpent Jormungand then targets

00:16:37.570 --> 00:16:40.430
and kills scores of Avengers.

00:16:40.430 --> 00:16:45.400
Soon only a handful of heroes still live,
as they decide to take on Jormungand despite

00:16:45.400 --> 00:16:47.380
the incredibly long odds.

00:16:47.380 --> 00:16:49.750
Amazingly, their boldness pays off.

00:16:49.750 --> 00:16:54.600
By taking the fight to Jormungand, the team
ends up in a position to find Mjolnir amongst

00:16:54.600 --> 00:16:58.800
the rubble, and Black Widow then grabs Thor's
abandoned hammer.

00:16:58.800 --> 00:17:03.850
She's evidently been made worthy by her time
fighting to forestall the end of humanity,

00:17:03.850 --> 00:17:08.329
and thus she can hoist the hammer skyward
and become the new God of Thunder.

00:17:08.329 --> 00:17:13.909
While the book only briefly shows her efforts,
Nick Fury's narration confirms that she indeed

00:17:13.909 --> 00:17:16.879
carried the day, and rather spectacularly
at that.

00:17:16.879 --> 00:17:19.569
"I want you to meet Agent Romanoff."

00:17:21.169 --> 00:17:25.400
X-Men's Rogue has been a fan favorite for
so long that newer readers might not know

00:17:25.400 --> 00:17:29.750
that she used to run with villains like the
Brotherhood of Evil Mutants.

00:17:29.750 --> 00:17:35.160
During that time, she even took on Carol Danvers
and permanently absorbed her abilities, like

00:17:35.160 --> 00:17:37.049
flight and super strength.

00:17:37.049 --> 00:17:38.049
What If...?

00:17:38.049 --> 00:17:40.220
#66, entitled "What If...

00:17:40.220 --> 00:17:44.350
Rogue Possessed the Powers of Thor," took
readers back to this era.

00:17:44.350 --> 00:17:48.760
After breaking out of prison with her fellow
Brotherhood members, Rogue and the other mutants

00:17:48.760 --> 00:17:52.289
find the Avengers ready to put them back in
their cells.

00:17:52.289 --> 00:17:57.320
Rogue absorbs the powers of Thor, who falls
into a coma and dies soon after.

00:17:57.320 --> 00:18:02.659
Now permanently possessing the powers of a
god, Rogue briefly falls into cahoots with

00:18:02.659 --> 00:18:03.659
Loki.

00:18:03.659 --> 00:18:07.850
Persuading her to help him kill Odin, the
God of Mischief mounts a rebellion.

00:18:07.850 --> 00:18:12.980
He sends Rogue and his troops to invade Asgard,
and things look pretty desperate until Thor

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:15.480
approaches Rogue on the astral plane.

00:18:15.480 --> 00:18:19.559
He convinces her that she can still be a hero
regardless of her past.

00:18:19.559 --> 00:18:25.149
So she accepts her new role as Goddess of
Thunder, routs Loki's forces, and gains acceptance

00:18:25.149 --> 00:18:26.450
from the gods and the Avengers.

00:18:27.769 --> 00:18:32.030
In the Disney+ animated series What If...?,
the episode "What If...

00:18:32.030 --> 00:18:33.450
Thor Were An Only Child?"

00:18:33.450 --> 00:18:40.049
sees the God of Thunder as an immortal partier
who can also nonetheless still wield his hammer.

00:18:40.049 --> 00:18:44.540
Without Loki to make his life miserable or
inspire him to protect others, he's lived

00:18:44.540 --> 00:18:47.970
a charmed life devoid of consequence or responsibility.

00:18:47.970 --> 00:18:53.450
As such, he's a charming but reckless moron
who hops from planet to planet throwing parties

00:18:53.450 --> 00:18:57.600
that are so intense that they end up ravaging
multiple worlds.

00:18:57.600 --> 00:19:02.179
After Thor arrives on Earth, things finally
start to change when Jane Foster helps him

00:19:02.179 --> 00:19:07.570
see the value of humanity and Captain Marvel
keeps his destructive impulses focused on

00:19:07.570 --> 00:19:08.570
her.

00:19:08.570 --> 00:19:13.019
In the end, the heroes of Earth manage to
save the planet in a manner both silly and

00:19:13.019 --> 00:19:14.019
logical.

00:19:14.019 --> 00:19:18.520
As it turns out, the best way to stop a man-child
in his tracks is by calling his mother.

00:19:19.520 --> 00:19:20.550
"Oh, hello, Mother, good to see you.

00:19:20.550 --> 00:19:21.550
Welcome to our study group."

00:19:21.550 --> 00:19:22.550
Wonder Woman

00:19:22.550 --> 00:19:23.550
Yes, even DC characters can be worthy of Mjolnir.

00:19:23.550 --> 00:19:28.629
During the blockbuster DC versus Marvel event,
cosmic forces pitted heroes from both universes

00:19:28.629 --> 00:19:30.120
against each other.

00:19:30.120 --> 00:19:35.149
After Thor loses his hammer while battling
DC's Captain Marvel, Wonder Woman then comes

00:19:35.149 --> 00:19:36.649
across Mjolnir.

00:19:36.649 --> 00:19:41.059
She's able to lift it and quickly absorb the
powers of the God of Thunder, emerging from

00:19:41.059 --> 00:19:43.649
the lightning in a new costume, ready for
a fight.

00:19:43.649 --> 00:19:49.190
But when her chosen opponent Storm arrives,
she quickly discards the hammer in the name

00:19:49.190 --> 00:19:54.200
of a fair and honorable fight and promptly
gets wrecked by the mutant.

00:19:54.200 --> 00:19:58.799
Considering that she's fighting for the very
existence of the DC universe, it might seem

00:19:58.799 --> 00:20:02.520
odd that Wonder Woman would so quickly cede
an advantage.

00:20:02.520 --> 00:20:07.280
However, it's worth noting that the results
of the crossover were based on fan voting.

00:20:07.280 --> 00:20:11.970
So perhaps the creators felt it was far too
unrealistic to give Storm her fan-affirmed

00:20:11.970 --> 00:20:18.420
victory over Wonder Woman when the Justice
Leaguer had both her own power and Thor's.

